 ### Exact Lattice Grid
-Exact Lattice Grid replaces octree-based brick sizing with an exact lattice defined by `gridDims`, allowing specific block counts that were previously unreachable due to scalar `cellEdge` sizing [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rigid block count stepping in octree structures. Steps: 1. Set real `gridDims`/stride on plan so `chunkAtVoxel` indexes it. 2. Axis grows when brick would exceed `deviceLimit` (`emitBrick` clamps oversize texture). 3. Callers read built plan's own `gridDims` back [S1, unofficial]. Pitfall: Previous `chunkVolumeMultiLOD` sized bricks from scalar `cellEdge`, so counts stepped 2, 8, 12, 16, 27, 4 on `hoa_heart` L5; 4 or 9 were unreachable. `maxBricks` only coarsened by raising level floor, fighting level control [S1, unofficial].
+Exact Lattice Grid replaces octree-based brick sizing with an exact lattice defined by `gridDims`, allowing specific block counts that were previously unreachable due to scalar `cellEdge` sizing [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rigid block count stepping in octree structures [S1, unofficial]. Steps: 1. Set real `gridDims`/stride on plan so `chunkAtVoxel` indexes it [S1, unofficial]. 2. Axis grows when brick would exceed `deviceLimit` (`emitBrick` clamps oversize texture) [S1, unofficial]. 3. Callers read built plan's own `gridDims` back [S1, unofficial]. Pitfall: Previous `chunkVolumeMultiLOD` sized bricks from scalar `cellEdge`, so counts stepped 2, 8, 12, 16, 27, 4 on `hoa_heart` L5; 4 or 9 were unreachable. `maxBricks` only coarsened by raising level floor, fighting level control [S1, unofficial].
 
